<section class="phero"><div class="phero-media"><img src="/assets/img/photos/cape-coast.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/cape-coast-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/cape-coast.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="900" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><a href="/towns-we-cover/">Towns we cover</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span aria-current="page">Biddeford</span></nav><p class="kicker">Southern Coast · York County</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Biddeford, Maine</h1><p class="lede">Biddeford pairs huge brick mill conversions along the Saco River with exposed shorefront at the Pool, Hills Beach and Fortunes Rocks. We help owners and associations challenge underpaid claims on both kinds of property.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-coral" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg><span>Call (844) 537-1427</span></a><a class="btn btn-line light" href="/reach-us/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="spec"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>York County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Southern Coast</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose"><div class="snap"><h2>Biddeford at a glance</h2><dl>
<div><dt>County</dt><dd>York County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Southern Coast</dd></div>
<div class="wide"><dt>Neighborhoods and villages</dt><dd><ul class="chips"><li>Downtown Main Street</li><li>Mill District</li><li>Biddeford Pool</li><li>Hills Beach</li><li>Fortunes Rocks</li><li>Granite Point</li><li>Saco</li></ul></dd></div>
<div class="wide"><dt>Housing mix</dt><dd>Massive brick textile mills along the Saco River now converted to apartments, studios and offices, wood-frame tenements and duplexes downtown, and oceanfront cottages and year-round homes at Biddeford Pool, Hills Beach and Fortunes Rocks.</dd></div>
<div class="wide"><dt>Common claim risks</dt><dd><ul class="chips coral"><li>Seawall and surf</li><li>Nor’easter wind</li><li>Mill building water</li><li>Ice dams</li></ul></dd></div></dl>
<h3>Storms on record</h3><ol class="mini-storms"><li><b>Jan 2024</b><span><strong>Back-to-back coastal storms.</strong> Surf undermined the Fortunes Rocks seawall; several shorefront homes were declared unsafe.</span></li><li><b>Mar 2024</b><span><strong>March 10 coastal storm.</strong> High tide and wind hit the same Biddeford Pool and Fortunes Rocks shoreline still under repair.</span></li><li><b>May 2006</b><span><strong>Mother’s Day flood.</strong> More than a foot of rain in places caused widespread flooding and damage across York County.</span></li></ol></div>
<h2>Two very different Biddefords</h2>
<p>Downtown Biddeford is defined by its mills. The Pepperell Mill campus and its neighbors along the Saco River are massive brick buildings, many now converted to apartments, condos, studios and restaurants. A few miles east, the city turns into shoreline: Biddeford Pool, Hills Beach, Fortunes Rocks and Granite Point, where cottages and year-round homes sit close to the surf. An insurance appraiser in Biddeford has to price both a fourth-floor water loss in a mill condo and wave damage to a shingle-style cottage.</p>
<h2>Shorefront losses after 2024</h2>
<p>The January 10 and 13, 2024 storms hit the Biddeford shoreline hard. Surf undermined the seawall along Fortunes Rocks, roads washed out, and several shorefront homes were declared unsafe. The March 10, 2024 storm then struck the same stretch while repairs were still under way. Three storms in three months create a real challenge: carriers may argue that damage from one event was really from another, or that it pre-dated the policy period.</p>
<p>Wave wash and storm surge are flood, and homeowners policies typically exclude them. Wind damage to roofs, siding and windows from the same storms is usually a property claim. Good dated photos after each storm make the difference when separating the two. Our <a href="/appraisal-work/noreaster-hurricane-appraisal/">nor’easter and hurricane appraisal</a> page explains how we handle mixed-cause coastal losses.</p>
<h2>Inside the mills</h2>
<p>Mill conversions bring association master policies, unit-owner policies and commercial tenants under one roof. A sprinkler or pipe failure on an upper floor can run through heavy timber floors into several units and a business below. Questions about who owns which piece of the building come first and are decided by the policies and association documents; appraisal then sets the amount. Biddeford associations can read about our <a href="/appraisal-work/commercial-condo-association-appraisal/">commercial and condo association appraisal</a> work.</p>
<h2>Pricing realities in York County</h2>
<ul>
<li>Shorefront jobs often need engineering, permitting and seasonal timing that estimates leave out.</li>
<li>Cedar shingle siding and trim on older cottages are hard to match after partial damage.</li>
<li>Mill repairs involve masonry, tall ceilings, large windows and lift access.</li>
<li>After a regional storm, York County contractors book out for months, which raises prices.</li>
</ul>
<p>Mill-era duplexes and tenements downtown add another layer. Many still heat with oil, share plumbing between units, and have plaster walls under later paneling. A frozen pipe or puffback in one of these buildings spreads into several apartments, and the estimate has to follow it. Owners at Biddeford Pool and Hills Beach often have seasonal homes that sit empty in winter, where freeze-ups raise vacancy questions under the policy.</p>
<p>The May 2006 Mother’s Day flood is another reminder that inland water can be as costly as the surf. Whatever the cause, a Biddeford insurance appraiser can only resolve the amount of loss. Coverage questions and policy deadlines belong with a Maine attorney.</p>

<h2>Appraisal work for Biddeford properties</h2>
<p>Every Maine Insurance Appraiser service is available in Biddeford and the surrounding towns, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/appraisal-work/homeowner-dispute-appraisal/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-work/noreaster-hurricane-appraisal/">Nor’easter &amp; Hurricane Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-work/water-damage-loss-appraisal/">Water Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-work/ice-dam-snow-load-appraisal/">Ice Dam &amp; Snow Load Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-work/fallen-tree-limb-appraisal/">Fallen Tree Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/appraisal-work/carrier-estimate-line-review/">Insurance Estimate Review</a></li></ul>
<h2>Biddeford questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>My Fortunes Rocks home was hit by storms in January and March 2024. How do I keep the claims straight?</summary><p>Use dated photos, contractor notes and any carrier inspection reports for each storm. Clear records make it easier to show which damage came from which event and under which claim.</p></details><details><summary>Does appraisal apply to a mill condo water loss in Biddeford?</summary><p>Yes, once the policies establish who covers which part of the building. The association’s master policy and the unit owner’s policy each have their own appraisal clauses.</p></details><details><summary>Is wave damage to my Biddeford Pool cottage covered under homeowners insurance?</summary><p>Wave wash and surge are usually treated as flood and excluded. Wind damage to the roof and siding is often covered, so review both your homeowners and flood policies.</p></details></div>
